{
  "item": "Object40",
  "mu_name": "Object40",
  "mu_name_from": "Noria's object slot 39, which is the model index: every world but Lorencia runs its objects in one straight sequence, so type N is Object{N+1}.bmd and there is no friendlier name in the client than the number.",
  "world": "noria",
  "object_type": 39,
  "placements": 1,
  "profile": "world",
  "sheets": {
    "htht01": "nr_htht01.png",
    "yellow_jewel": "nr_yellow_jewel.png",
    "ob3": "nr_ob3.png"
  },
  "sheet_from": "Data/Object4/*.OZJ and .OZT, from MuMain, decoded under an nr_ prefix. The prefix is load-bearing for the reason the ground's is: assets/textures is one flat pool for every world, and yellow_jewel.png was already taken by an item.",
  "sheet_materials": {
    "htht01": "plank",
    "yellow_jewel": "lamplight",
    "ob3": "skin"
  },
  "material_note": "htht01: a props atlas: crates, boards, a banded chest, a shield and a wheel.\nyellow_jewel: eight pixels of a yellow gem.\nob3: the Chaos Goblin's own hide - purple with orange runes, the same bytes as Data/NPC/ob3.OZJ (see MixNpc01). Worn by the goblins that crew the machine, so skin and not plaster. It was taken for a stray reference render until the md5s matched.",
  "why_this_one": "Object40, Object41, Object42 and Object43 are one thing: all four stand at 18100,10450, a few units apart in height, and together they are the Chaos Machine beside the Chaos Goblin. This is the body of it, with the two goblins on its near side.",
